 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# RaspTank Initial Hardware Validation Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intended for a safe, guided first-pass validation of the refactored hardware wrappers.\n",
    "\n",
    "Important notes:\n",
    "- This notebook does NOT attempt to run the entire robot autonomously.\n",
    "- The goals are to validate imports, object wiring, and symbolic behavior in a controlled way.\n",
    "- For real hardware tests, use a safe, stationary setup and keep the robot on a stand or table.\n",
    "- For anything that moves the robot, do so slowly and with a clear stop plan.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is meant to be educational and transparent. It is a first-pass validation environment.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# This cell imports the refactored package and checks that the package root can be imported.\n",
    "# If this fails, it usually means the local package path is not correctly set up.\n",
    "\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "print('Python version:', sys.version)\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import rasptank\n",
    "    print('IMPORT_OK: rasptank package loaded successfully')\n",
    "    print('PACKAGE_EXPORTS:', [name for name in dir(rasptank) if not name.startswith('_')])\n",
    "except Exception as exc:\n",
    "    print('IMPORT_ERROR:', repr(exc))\n",
    "    raise\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# This cell validates that the hardware layer classes can be imported without trying to\n",
    "# initialize actual Raspberry Pi hardware.\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from rasptank.hardware.motors import MotorController\n",
    "    from rasptank.hardware.servos import ServoController\n",
    "    from rasptank.hardware.ultrasonic import UltrasonicSensor\n",
    "    from rasptank.hardware.leds import LEDStrip\n",
    "    from rasptank.hardware.display import OledDisplay\n",
    "    from rasptank.tank import RaspTank\n",
    "    print('IMPORT_OK: all hardware and robot classes imported')\n",
    "except Exception as exc:\n",
    "    print('IMPORT_ERROR:', repr(exc))\n",
    "    raise\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 1: Motor validation\n",
    "\n",
    "The motor layer is the first thing to test because it is the core robot behavior. The goal here is to\n",
    "verify that the wrapper still reflects the original direction logic from `server/move.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook intentionally avoids running a real robot unless the user is in a safe, physically verified setup.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# This is a symbolic validation. It does not move the robot.\n",
    "# It ensures the controller object can be created and that its expected methods exist.\n",
    "\n",
    "controller = MotorController(use_gpio=False)\n",
    "print('MOTOR_CONTROLLER_CREATED:', type(controller).__name__)\n",
    "print('HAS_FORWARD:', hasattr(controller, 'forward'))\n",
    "print('HAS_BACKWARD:', hasattr(controller, 'backward'))\n",
    "print('HAS_TURN_LEFT:', hasattr(controller, 'turn_left'))\n",
    "print('HAS_TURN_RIGHT:', hasattr(controller, 'turn_right'))\n",
    "print('HAS_STOP:', hasattr(controller, 'stop'))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# This checks the core public robot object, which is the main user-facing API we want to expose.\n",
    "\n",
    "tank = RaspTank()\n",
    "print('RASP_TANK_CREATED:', type(tank).__name__)\n",
    "print('HAS_FORWARD:', hasattr(tank, 'forward'))\n",
    "print('HAS_BACKWARD:', hasattr(tank, 'backward'))\n",
    "print('HAS_TURN_LEFT:', hasattr(tank, 'turn_left'))\n",
    "print('HAS_TURN_RIGHT:', hasattr(tank, 'turn_right'))\n",
    "print('HAS_STOP:', hasattr(tank, 'stop'))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 2: Servo validation\n",
    "\n",
    "The servo wrapper is based on the original PCA9685 design. This stage confirms that the abstraction\n",
    "looks like the original hardware configuration and that the channel map is explicit.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# This tests the configuration structure without trying to move any servos.\n",
    "servo = ServoController(address=0x40, busnum=1)\n",
    "print('SERVO_CONTROLLER_CREATED:', type(servo).__name__)\n",
    "print('CHANNEL_KEYS:', sorted(servo.channels.keys()))\n",
    "for channel, cfg in servo.channels.items():\n",
    "    print(f'Channel {channel}: init={cfg[\'init\']}, min={cfg[\'min\']}, max={cfg[\'max\']}, direction={cfg[\'direction\']}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 3: Ultrasonic validation\n",
    "\n",
    "This checks the sensor wrapper and confirms that the original trigger/echo pin configuration is preserved.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sensor = UltrasonicSensor()\n",
    "print('ULTRASONIC_TRIGGER_PIN:', sensor.trigger_pin)\n",
    "print('ULTRASONIC_ECHO_PIN:', sensor.echo_pin)\n",
    "print('HAS_DISTANCE_METHOD:', hasattr(sensor, 'distance'))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 4: LED and display validation\n",
    "\n",
    "These are safe informational checks. They validate the presence of the wrappers and their expected methods.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "led = LEDStrip(count=16, pin=12)\n",
    "print('LED_STRIP_CREATED:', type(led).__name__)\n",
    "print('LED_COUNT:', led.count)\n",
    "print('HAS_COLOR_WIPE:', hasattr(led, 'color_wipe'))\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE TO USER:\n",
    "# The actual LED strip is not executed here. This is just a wrapper validation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "display = OledDisplay(port=1, address=0x3C)\n",
    "print('OLED_CREATED:', type(display).__name__)\n",
    "print('HAS_SHOW:', hasattr(display, 'show'))\n",
    "print('HAS_CLOSE:', hasattr(display, 'close'))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 5: Diagnostics summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this notebook is not to prove the robot is fully operational on its first run.\n",
    "The goal is to detect obvious wiring or import issues before any real hardware movement test begins.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intentionally explicit about its limits. That makes it safer and easier to learn from.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
